# Which control file applies depends on the build stage and the series:
#
#  - The Launchpad recipe builds and pdebuild install the Build-Depends of
#    THIS file before debian/rules ever runs, so it has to be satisfiable on
#    every Ubuntu series the PPA targets.
#  - debian/rules then copies debian/control.ubuntu.ppa over it on Ubuntu 24.04
#    and earlier, and debian/control.debian on Debian, before the source
#    package is generated. Those copies decide what the binary build installs.
#  - On Ubuntu 26.04 and later this file is used as it is: onnxruntime comes
#    from the Ubuntu archive, and the PPA carries no openvino, onert (nnfw),
#    tvm or pytorch build for those series.
#
# One consequence on Ubuntu 24.04 and earlier: dpkg-buildpackage checks the
# build dependencies of THIS file before debian/rules runs, so a plain
# dpkg-buildpackage there passes that check and then fails at meson configure
# on the openvino that debian/rules still enables. Build with pbuilder, as the
# PPA does, and the legacy build dependencies are the ones that get installed.
Source: nnstreamer
Section: libs
Priority: optional
